# 303 long notes on SEQ (#33): hold a step and press a later one, and the note lasts to it (ties
# between); its last step again: one step. KNOB 2 (a step a turn) walks NOTE, LEN 2, LEN 3 ... and SLIDE into the
# next note.
wait 300
turn ALGO 2
tap SEQ
key w2 down
tapkey w5
key w2 up
expect gate0.2 1
expect gate0.3 2
expect gate0.4 2
expect gate0.5 2
expect gate0.6 0
# shorter: the ties after it rest
key w2 down
tapkey w3
key w2 up
expect gate0.3 2
expect gate0.4 0
expect gate0.5 0
# its last step again: one step
key w2 down
tapkey w3
key w2 up
expect gate0.2 1
expect gate0.3 0
# KNOB 2 with a note at step 8: LEN 2 ... LEN 6, then SLIDE (ties to step 7, which slides into 8)
tapkey w8
key w2 down
spin K2 1
expect gate0.3 2
expect gate0.4 0
spin K2 1
spin K2 1
spin K2 1
spin K2 1
expect gate0.7 2
expect slide0.7 0
spin K2 1
expect gate0.7 2
expect slide0.7 1
# back a step: LEN 6, the slide gone
spin K2 -1
expect slide0.7 0
expect gate0.7 2
key w2 up
expect gate0.8 1
